(Probe B from the bug report: `but if` must work with append in loop expansion,
not just in the plain form.  The default action appends the loop variable; the
branch appends 0 when the variable is even.)

a list called source is [1, 2, 3].
a list called dest is [].
append each n from source to dest, but if n modulo 2 is equal to 0 append 0.
print dest.
